{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>If he offers it as a thanksgiving.</b> If for a matter of thanksgiving for a miracle that was done for him — such as those who go down to the sea and those who travel through deserts and those imprisoned and a sick person who recovered — for they must give thanks, for it is written of them ״יוֹדוּ לַה' חַסְדּוֹ וְנִפְלְאוֹתָיו לִבְנֵי אָדָם״ and ״וְיִזְבְּחוּ זִבְחֵי תוֹדָה״ (Psalms 107) — if for one of these he vowed such shelamim, they are shelamim of thanksgiving, and they require bread as stated in the passage, and they are eaten only for a day and a night, as is explicit here." "<b>And he shall bring with the sacrifice of thanksgiving.</b> Four kinds of bread — חַלּוֹת and רְקִיקִין and רְבוּכָה, three kinds of matzah, and it is written ״עַל חַלֹּת לֶחֶם חָמֵץ״ etc.; and each and every kind is ten loaves — so it is explicit in Menachot, and its measure is five Jerusalem se'ah, which are six wilderness measures, twenty esronot (Menachot 76)." "<b>Soaked.</b> Bread boiled in hot water completely."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:29.439752861Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}